@vsm 1.0
// calibration_batch.spec.vsm — AXIS-1 calibration nodes (the ✗/◐ instruments).
// Runs pattern(instrument_calibration_loop) P1-P5 per node. Frame: calibration_autonomy_strategy.vsm.
// author: Claude/Fable 2026-07-03 (rmw3 ratified the strategy). owner per node below.

spec(CALIBRATION-BATCH-1) {

  invariant: "no autonomous loop is closed on any instrument until it PASSES P3 (discriminates)."

  node(CALIBRATE-ENTROPY):   // ✗ saturated — [O] diagnose → DS [S] impl. priority=alta.
    problem:
      "h_t reads ~1.95/2.0 (h_max=log2(4)=2) and entropy_phase='degen' ALWAYS (live tick 47 + every prior
       tick). The instrument does NOT discriminate — it is pinned at max. persist-p (ENTROPY P2-A) fixed the
       restart RESET, not the chronic saturation."
    exercise_P2:
      "drive the kernel toward a LOW-entropy state and observe: (a) inject/force a concentrated p (one bin
       dominant) OR run a regime where p_eq is non-uniform; (b) watch whether h_t drops and entropy_phase
       leaves 'degen'. If h_t CANNOT be moved below h_max·0.7 → saturated/broken."
    diagnosed_2026_07_03:   // [O] Claude — CONFIRMED (computed), no longer a hypothesis:
      "ENERGIES=[0,0.5,1,1.5]; p_eq(kt=1,idle)=[0.455,0.276,0.167,0.102] ⇒ the ATTRACTOR entropy is
       h_eq=1.796 bits (of h_max=2.0) — NOT uniform, a real Boltzmann equilibrium. VERDICT = BOTH:
       (H1) the high-entropy attractor is REAL and INTENDED (the EXP-LY-01 equilibrium — do NOT touch it).
       (H2) the PHASE THRESHOLDS are MIS-CALIBRATED: 'degen' fires at h_t ≥ h_max·0.7 = 1.4, which is BELOW
            the healthy attractor (1.796) → the HEALTHY resting state is mislabeled 'degen' (normal-reads-
            anomalous — the exact tell). Live h_t~1.95 is even higher (p stuck near uniform h=2.0 by the slow
            0.99 relaxation + restarts; persist-p mitigates only the restart half)."
    fix_P4_P5:   // [S] — DO NOT touch the dynamics (λ_max=ln0.99 is load-bearing, EXP-LY-01):
      "Recalibrate the entropy PHASE THRESHOLDS to be RELATIVE to h_eq, not the absolute 0.7·h_max. Compute
       h_eq = H(boltzmann_p_eq(kt_eff)) each tick; set: stasis = h_t ≤ h_rest·1.1; inhale = h_rest < h_t < h_eq+ε;
       degen = h_t ≥ h_eq + margin (a GENUINE excursion ABOVE the attractor — e.g. sustained pressure flattening
       p_eq toward uniform). VERIFY: the healthy resting state reads inhale/stasis (NOT degen); a real high-entropy
       push reads degen; the phase now DISCRIMINATES."
    rmw3_decision: "recommended/near-trivial: KEEP the attractor (EXP-LY-01), recalibrate the thresholds. Low-risk
                    (does not touch the contraction). Effectively a yes."
    owner: "DS [S] — diagnosis DONE, fix is a threshold recalibration. files: kernel_step.rs (phase_str)."

  node(CALIBRATE-TRUST):   // ✗ suspect (reads 1.0 always) — DS [S], mostly VERIFY. priority=alta.
    problem:
      "trust=1.0, min_axis≈0.9996, breach=False on every live tick. Unknown whether it DISCRIMINATES —
       i.e. whether it drops on a real breach and recovers. (EXP-TRUST-01 tested this partially: shared λ=0.10,
       behavioral noise does not leak to structural; but live discrimination is unverified.)"
    exercise_P2:
      "on LXC 108 (sandbox) OR a guarded window, inject a CONTROLLED breach on each axis in turn —
       structural (drop a structural signal), behavioral (σ=0.10 noise), communicative (broker gap),
       predictive (projection error) — and record the trust trajectory."
    discriminate_P3:
      "PASS iff each axis's trust drops measurably under its own breach, does NOT drop under unrelated
       breaches (isolation, per EXP-TRUST-01), and recovers when the breach clears (λ=0.10 timescale)."
    outcome:
      "if PASS → mark trust CALIBRATED (no fix, just the verification we never ran live). If a breach does
       NOT move the axis (pinned) → recalibrate that axis's sensitivity. Either way the census node closes."
    owner: "DS [S] (exercise + record); Claude reviews the discrimination verdict."
    files: [projects/vsf-nucleus/src/... (trust axes), "reuse EXP-TRUST-01 harness"]

  node(VERIFY-STASIS-COS + VERIFY-VARIETY):   // ◐ — DS [S], lightweight. priority=media.
    task: "exercise stasis_cos (nucleus) + variety.delta across perturbation (load, drift) and confirm each
           VARIES with the state and that a typical state reads healthy. Quick discrimination checks; likely PASS.
           margin_free: verify post-BINDING-DIAG it now discriminates (binding constraint changes with state)."
    owner: "DS [S]."

  handoff:
    "DS: after the current backlog, run CALIBRATE-TRUST + the VERIFY nodes (they are exercises, low-risk).
     CALIBRATE-ENTROPY waits on Claude's P3/P4 diagnosis + rmw3's kernel-semantics decision (H1 vs H2).
     Each node closed → update the census in calibration_autonomy_strategy.vsm. When all ✗/◐ pass P3,
     AXIS 1 is done and AXIS 2 (autonomous loops) opens on the calibrated instruments."
  status: "SPEC ready — Axis-1 batch. TRUST + VERIFY hand to DS [S]; ENTROPY gated on Claude diagnosis + rmw3."
}
